    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d793">

                <pb facs="1154" n="1140" sameAs="frus:frus1947v05/pg1140"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/8–2247: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Embassy in the United Kingdom
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-08-22T14:00:00-04:00">August 22, 1947—2
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3633. For Ambassador. Deptel 3623 of Aug 22.
                    We have just been informed informally by British Emb that Brit Govt finds itself
                    unable to alter its plans and intends to return refugees from <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Exodus</hi> to Germany.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d793-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Wide sections of the American public opinion are being aroused at reports that
                    Brit intend to send Jewish refugees back to country in which Jews have suffered
                    such savage persecution. Protests to-White House and Dept are piling up. If Brit
                    persist in carrying out intentions much harm will undoubtedly be done to their
                    position in US. Please therefore take up matter at once with Brit Govt at high
                    level in a more formal manner than that suggested in telegram under ref. More in
                    subsequent telegram.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d793-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d793-f1" n="1" xml:id="d793-f1-content">
                <p>In a memorandum of his conversation with the First Secretary of the British
                    Embassy (Bromley) on August 22, the Assistant Chief of the Division of Near
                    Eastern Affairs (Mattison) set forth the British position as being “literally
                    true that they had no other place to take them that would not take time and
                    considerable expense to prepare.” (.867 N.01/8–2247)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d793-f2" n="2" xml:id="d793-f2-content">
                <p>Background data was provided to Ambassador Douglas in telegram 3634, August 22, 7
                    p. m. (867N.01/8–2247).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
